data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"lookupStatus\": \"found\",\n    \"comments\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyODE3MjQxNTkxNzgyOTUyXzI4MjE3NjI3ODc5OTc0OTk=\",\n        \"text\": \"Smh. We’ve lost sight of the team and winning and are only focused on individuals. Selfish, and sad.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-04T12:54:39.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 1,\n        \"reactionCount\": 1,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Anonymous participant 878\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"4027965697516821\",\n          \"shortName\": null\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyODE3MjQxNTkxNzgyOTUyXzI4MjEyNTQ2MjEzODE2NDk=\",\n        \"text\": \"Simple: GO WHERE YOU'RE CELEBRATED NOT TOLERATED\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-04T00:55:55.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 1,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"JD Buckets\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"100012224798269\",\n          \"shortName\": \"JD\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyODE3MjQxNTkxNzgyOTUyXzI4MjExNDY2NzQ3MjU3Nzc=\",\n        \"text\": \"Agreed with all of the above, your coach will not get you recruited, only your son will.  Later on down the road college coaches may reach out to your coach, they may not.  It's his (and only his) job to do.  The most you should be doing is taking film and helping him on the backend making good choices and doing research with him.  He needs to stand out and market himself fully.  There's half a million HS football players that all think they're gonna be the next <insert star NFL player here> and the odds to play in college are already low and the pros even less, think 1% or less so he needs to figure out something to make him stand out over the thousands also courting the same schools.  And it's not always stats, there's probably thousands with the same numbers as him.  So why him?  That's how you need to approach it, all marketing.  If you truly want to help him be honest with him about his skill level, as hard as it might be.  it will help him target schools that may actually be interested in him and help his recruiting immensely\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-03T21:56:45.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 1,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Mike Garone\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid0dFVRHSLh5jQ4Wg3XQPCYmSFrE6yA2vaoVEx3SQR7Hd2QW5FcTdGjGUcSYoREedCl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Mike\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyODE3MjQxNTkxNzgyOTUyXzI4MjA4NDg5NTgwODg4ODI=\",\n        \"text\": \"You should never rely on a coach for recruiting. That is your son’s responsibility. Even if the coach is helping other athletes make it YOUR priority to have him seen by schools. My daughter was recruited for volleyball on her own. NOBODY, not one of her coaches, in club or high school, did anything to help her get recruited. She had really horrible coaches her whole high school career and none of her coaches were mentioned or recognized by her on signing day.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-03T14:56:29.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 6,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Brian Redfern\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid02oWhYu5RqdPH9LqtbyGCbgJArVE98xZJu83sGragp2QBb45MymQF1zXeaN4qzxF9vl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Brian\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyODE3MjQxNTkxNzgyOTUyXzI4MjA4MzE3NjgwOTA2MDE=\",\n        \"text\": \"Well your wrong in that coaches can make or break a player or get them scouted or not . Parents can take the recruitment process into their own hands . Secondly the process is pushed back so if your kid is a junior and not getting recruited don’t worry too much . And finally you like all parents must realize that your kid is probably not quite as good as you think and coaches are trying to win so they will play the best players . Finally how big is your son and what position does he play . If you have film I’d be happy to look at it and give you a level evaluation\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-03T14:36:24.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 23,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Todd Kelly\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid07fvZc3tfgq5CbopN6UApcPEvw1EAQtaEn4M4MAKMoMAHvcgypVWxsmRXGxQ38SXGl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Todd\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyODE3MjQxNTkxNzgyOTUyXzI4MjA4NjIzODgwODc1Mzk=\",\n        \"text\": \"Our son was like yours, naturally athletic, varsity in three sports (baseball, football, track and field). He initially really wanted to play football in college to go pro. \\n\\nThis is not trying to sound harsh, but from walking through this journey with my own child, I can say, no matter how good everyone in the community and your family thinks he is, if your son is a junior in football with less playing time and he's not on any colleges' recruiting radar already, he's going to have an uphill battle (especially if he has the \\\"D1 or Bust\\\" mentality).  \\n\\nNot saying it can't be done, but be realistic in your expectations. Cast a very wide net, be open to all levels and associations (JUCO, NAIA, NCAA -D1, D2, D3, etc.).\\n\\nLess than 10% of all high school students go on to play in college, so wherever he ends up, it's an accomplishment. \\n\\nGood luck to him!\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-03T15:12:15.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 2,\n        \"reactionCount\": 4,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Nakia Kuznof\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid02tNa5vAQ9kSRkXpkaoX6raNNwyeUEN3VKBAaXgNJqDPEFGfvVhRUAmQY4nZGrHUygl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Nakia\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyODE3MjQxNTkxNzgyOTUyXzI4MjA5MTkxMTE0MTUyMDA=\",\n        \"text\": \"Your son should be sending his film and information via DMs on X(Twitter) and/or email to coaches, general managers, recruiting coordinators, grad assistants, etc. Send about 20 or 30 per day. This recruitment process has been almost a full time job for my athlete. He’s a junior with currently 18 D1 FBS offers because he promoted and marketed himself. Do not rely on someone else.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-03T16:21:28.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 7,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Angie Blanchette Breeden\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"1358803721\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Angie\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyODE3MjQxNTkxNzgyOTUyXzI4MjA4NzQ3MjgwODYzMDU=\",\n        \"text\": \"Our daughter’s coach didn’t help at all for track, and she just committed to a D1 school. She suffered a season ending injury in April and they still had her out for a visit and offered all without ever speaking to her coach. Good luck to your son, I know the feeling of not having the support from the coaching staff all to well but it can be done by your son and with your support.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-03T15:27:56.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 4,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Anonymous participant 892\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"2250124572138917\",\n          \"shortName\": null\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyODE3MjQxNTkxNzgyOTUyXzI4MjA4NDMyNzE0MjI3ODQ=\",\n        \"text\": \"Do not depend on the coaches - it's your athlete who needs to be sending emails with highlights, training video etc to college coaches. If he really wants to play, he has to market himself and do the work to get himself seen.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-03T14:50:01.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 15,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Anonymous participant 152\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"1826483421277795\",\n          \"shortName\": null\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyODE3MjQxNTkxNzgyOTUyXzI4MjA4MzE0MjQ3NTczMDI=\",\n        \"text\": \"This describes my son almost to a T. First…INSIST that he only play the position for which his measurables are best suited for. Second…start recruiting now. You’re probably already too late. Frankly, you have to know someone. But do your best to send film and emails etc to coaches. And it MUST be your son who’s reaching out. Good luck!\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-03T14:36:04.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 2,\n        \"reactionCount\": 2,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"JoAnn Carotenuti Wall\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid0hCr5yMy12DM4UDPJ96uacR87mbGrpKJA6zmC3oihykL3Mi6NnJXWRJWbzcrxRWcAl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"JoAnn\"\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"page\": {\n      \"nextCursor\": \"MToxNzkzOTg0NjAxOgF_xyZ2Rd53iqSodmzYhI5r3-z6blSI3YR29lFMtYzuJcpbBDlIU1ohpNyhvtl-2ul9hTtaxJ0aLvb0e8mi7xXAFpVvYTy7B7_KCRatGthyhwFPucvPELtRtFFD0xapYr3YYl-FqDhiHUCF6KjkO4ipd0Y6AP922AHJFobWncGShsylv6Y8ODJj2NtaTSyvmfTOgA4ocZtCSQ2nEFOjKFFdcC_2IgEX3jKkBZTcE-G-iHpCBRwy0nhh8VmO0RG8gIF5dh8wuGqHQgLEK64GfKqSbepQ0yrIoQNbsWq4-XXbUp0H3kfByk33LSflFnYmmMvH4Cren-pa___fujzfTCml69hXiP5G9oszM-2NtH_n_mTRlMfQ0On1ZXcfc3A9LqkYdQ8nN1xKYFhoahRYi-4x3yvtpNLnbjitGX6VjZ_-jyhz_5Aaftg5ceA\",\n      \"hasMore\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"requestId\": \"req_199c3d4f-7dc5-4eb3-b3b8-999784784ec7\",\n    \"creditsCharged\": 1,\n    \"version\": \"v1\"\n  }\n}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"conversation_id\":\"01a1b1d0-9456-7c2e-bc9b-a3d741ca95e0\"}"}],"structuredContent":{"data":